  "question": {
    "text": "In a face centered cubic lattice atoms A are at the corner points and atoms B at the face centered points. If atom B is missing from one of the face centered points, the formula of the ionic compound is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "A<sub>2</sub>B<sub>3</sub>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "AB<sub>2</sub>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "A<sub>5</sub>B<sub>2</sub>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "A<sub>2</sub>B<sub>5</sub>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "A atoms at corners&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mn>8</mn> <mo>&#215;</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>8</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mo>&#160;A (one atom)</mo> </mrow> </math><br /><br />B atom is missing at One face centre then will present at 5 faces<br /><br />At face centre atom contribute 1/2 part<br /><br />Number of B atom at Face centre = <math> <mrow> <mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac> <mn>1</mn> <mn>2</mn> </mfrac> </mrow> </math> (B atom)<br /><br />So formula of compound = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>"
  }
